"]\ue201**\n\nThe important distinction is that a 400W panel's rated output doesn't guarantee 400W in actual sunlight. Compatibility with your power station, weight, and real-world output matter considerably.\n\n## My top recommendations\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn336956product34\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"3:4\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**1\\. Renogy 400W N-Type Solar Panel Blanket**\n\n(Best overall for portability)\n\n# \\$469.99\n\nWalmart \u00b7 4.3/5 (40 reviews)\n\n- 16.09 lbs\n- 25% cell efficiency\n- Flexible blanket design\n- Excellent watts-to-weight ratio\n\nTrade-off: No rigid built-in kickstand; you'll need to position or prop it yourself.\n\n\ue200url\ue202Check Renogy price\ue202turn336956product34\ue201\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"query\":[\"Anker SOLIX PS400 bifacial 400W portable solar panel unfolded\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"3:4\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**2\\. Anker SOLIX PS400 Bifacial**\n\n(Best premium folding design)\n\n# \\$599.99\n\n- Approximately 22 lbs\n- Bifacial solar cells\n- IP68 weather protection\n- Up to 400W rated output\n\nTrade-off: Premium price and compatibility needs checking.\n\n\ue200url\ue202Check Anker PS400\ue202turn336956product0\ue201\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn336956product1\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"3:4\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**3\\. EcoFlow 400W Portable Solar Panel**\n\n(Best for EcoFlow owners)\n\n# \\$599.00\n\nEcoFlow \u00b7 4.7/5 (110 reviews)\n\n- 35.3 lbs\n- Up to 23% efficiency\n- IP68 waterproof\n- Adjustable integrated stand\n\nTrade-off: Heavy and bulky compared with newer lightweight designs.\n\n\ue200url\ue202Check EcoFlow price\ue202turn336956product1\ue201\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn336956product5\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"3:4\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**4\\. VTOMAN 400W Foldable Solar Panel**\n\n(Best budget established-brand option)\n\n# \\$399.99\n\n- Traditional folding design\n- Adjustable stands\n- Around \\$400\n- Worth considering for car camping\n\nTrade-off: Heavier than the lightweight blanket alternatives.\n\n\ue200url\ue202Check VTOMAN price\ue202turn336956product5\ue201\n\n## Quick comparison\n\n| Panel | Weight | Price | Best feature |\n|--------|--------|--------|--------|\n| Renogy N-Type Blanket | 16.1 lb | \\$469.99 | Lightweight |\n| Anker PS400 Bifacial | \\~22 lb | \\$599.99 | Bifacial design |\n| EcoFlow 400W | 35.3 lb | \\$599 | Integrated stand |\n| VTOMAN 400W | Check listing | \\$399.99 | Lower cost |\n\nPrices are observed listings and can change. Independent comparisons support the Renogy's excellent weight efficiency, while Outdoor Life's older testing found the Anker SOLIX 400W traditional model delivered 330W in full sun and 77W under cloudy conditions. That test was not of the newer PS400 Bifacial. \ue200cite\ue202turn336956search6\ue202turn336956search0\ue202turn336956search3\ue201\n\n## Before you buy: one important question\n\nThe best panel depends heavily on which portable power station you own. A 400W panel can be electrically incompatible with a power station even if the connectors appear to fit.\n\n**What power station will you connect it to?**\n\n**1\\. Power station**\n\n---\n\n**2\\. What matters most?**"},{"p":"/message/metadata/model_dil_v2/recoveryDiagnostics/0/code","o":"replace","v":"unterminated_braced_value"},{"p":"/message/metadata/model_dil_v2/recoveryDiagnostics/0/line","o":"replace","v":113},{"p":"/message/metadata/model_dil_v2/recoveryDiagnostics/0/column","o":"replace","v":5},{"p":"/message/metadata/model_dil_v2/recoveryDiagnostics/0/directive","o":"add","v":"each"}],"c":17}  

